Evidence: `src/features/teams/sub_kpis/kpiConvergence.ts` (with tests in `__tests__/kpiConvergence.test.ts`). The honesty rules are stated at the top and enforced:

```ts
// Honesty rules: no pairing is invented (no production data → no gap, an
// explicit empty state); a production reading older than the sim is flagged as
// STALE rather than treated as the current truth
```

Mechanics: `splitChannels` partitions by `env`; each sim point takes the nearest-in-time production partner; `gap = sim − prod`; `normalized = |gap| / gapSpan(target, baseline, prodValue)` where a degenerate span yields `null` (never a fake ratio); `prodStaleDays` records partner staleness; the verdict compares first vs last normalized gap with `VERDICT_EPS = 0.02` and abstains (`'insufficient'`) below 2 normalizable runs.

Reusable anywhere a predicted series must be validated against sparse, irregular ground truth.

Evidence: `src/features/teams/sub_factory/passport/actionConfirmCatalog.ts`.

```ts
/** read = nothing is written · write = touches the repo or config ·
 *  agent = spawns a Claude session that can write once you answer it. */
export type ActionImpact = 'read' | 'write' | 'agent';
export interface ActionSpec { id; icon; tooltip; title; impact; summary; steps: string[]; boundaries: string[]; facts: ActionFact[]; confirmLabel; }
```

The header pins the sync contract: "Everything here must stay TRUE of the code paths in PassportActionsRow — ... If a flow changes, change its steps in the same edit." And `buildActionSpecs(name, root, populateLanes?)` takes the per-project lane verdicts late: "the populate action's steps are only honest if they say what THIS project's run would actually do ... omitting it falls back to the generic description used before the gates have loaded." Boundaries encode standing guarantees ("Credential VALUES never leave the vault", "The session changes nothing in the repo until you answer its prompts").

Consumed by `ActionConfirmModal.tsx`. Reusable for any app dispatching agents or destructive automation on the user's behalf.

Evidence: `src/features/teams/sub_factory/passport/improve/goldenStandard.ts`:

```ts
// The golden-standard RUBRIC — makes "golden" an explicit, tunable spec instead
// of magic numbers buried in the score weights.
export interface RubricDim {
  key: string; label: string; weight: number;
  pos: (p: AppPassport) => number;              // current attainment 0..1
  target: Record<Archetype, number>;             // per-archetype 0..1
